The standalone VS Code extension bundles Prettier 3 and Azure.Bicep.Core
0.47.16 with their transitive dependencies. The Prettier license is included
in licenses/PRETTIER-LICENSE.txt, and the Bicep license is included in
licenses/BICEP-LICENSE.txt inside the VSIX.
Prettier's transitive dependency notices ship in
licenses/PRETTIER-THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md.
Bicep is Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation and licensed under the MIT License:
https://github.com/Azure/bicep/blob/v0.47.16/LICENSE

The Bicep compiler is used as a dependency; this project is not affiliated with
or endorsed by Microsoft, GitHub, or the Prettier project.

Dependency versions are recorded in native/Bicep.Formatter/packages.lock.json
and package-lock.json in the source repository. Release builds include a
dependency license inventory in dist/bridge/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt.
